INV-hazov. Seven times between April and August a meta slot several writers
could reach held a single value, and the last writer silently erased the
earlier ones: INV-forim, the BUG-04/05 family, INV-zumin, INV-pojib,
INV-virat, the verify_claims caveat list, and a seventh found live while
filing this class item. Every one was fixed correctly, locally, and in a way
that did nothing to make the next one harder. That is a missing mechanism,
not a run of bad luck.

WHY THE EXISTING REGISTRY COULD NOT HAVE CAUGHT ANY OF THEM. axis_meta_keys
governs WHICH keys may exist and WHAT VOCABULARY their values draw from. It
is blind to ARITY by construction, and the offending write in INV-virat was
a correctly-spelled assignment of a registered key -- so a finished
conformance linter (the follow-on the registry's own docstring says it owes,
WI-vusot, still P4) would have waved it straight through. The gap was never
enforcement of the vocabulary rule; it was that no rule existed about how
many writers reach a slot.

MetaKeySpec gains write_discipline -- single_writer / merge_union /
producer_primary / refines / unaudited -- with a mandatory discipline_note
on every value that asserts something. write_meta_key() is the ONE place a
shared key is written, so the fold lives once instead of being re-derived
and re-forgotten per call site. io_boundary.py's INV-virat branch is gone:
"the producer's stamp survives" is now just what the key's declaration
MEANS, so there is no second place left to forget it.

UNAUDITED IS THE DEFAULT ON PURPOSE. Declaring single_writer wrongly buys a
FALSE assurance, which is worse than no assurance -- the INV-faput lesson,
where a mislabelled catalogue row bought a `confirmed`. The count is
reported as visible debt (82 of 87 keys) rather than hidden behind a
permissive default, and rule 2 fails CLOSED: a key a second writer can
demonstrably reach may not sit at the default.

THE DISCRIMINATOR WAS VALIDATED BEFORE IT WAS TRUSTED, and this is the part
that mattered. 80 registered keys are written by more than one MODULE. Only
FOUR are written both at construction and by post-hoc mutation -- and two of
those four are the io keys that produced INV-virat and INV-zumin. A
measurement that independently rediscovers both known defects is a control.
The module count would have reported 80 mostly-benign hits and taught
nobody anything: each of 26 linkers writing framework_dispatch on edges it
constructs itself has 26 writers and zero collisions. Module count is not
collision count, and the first draft of this census reported the wrong one.

THE SEVENTH INSTANCE, found by the census and fixed here.
framework_patterns.enrich_symbols assigned pattern matches over the top of
Symbol.meta["concepts"], so a symbol the ANALYZER had stamped (python's
main_guard, bash's shell_script, go's middleware) lost that fact the moment
any framework pattern matched it. Measured with the control firing on both
runs:

  before  [{'concept': 'producer_fact'}] -> [{'concept': 'route'}]
  after   both present

The same file already contained a hand-rolled union in its OTHER concepts
writer -- one fact, two homes, one of them wrong. Both now route through the
single fold.

INV-FORIM IS CLOSED BY CONSTRUCTION RATHER THAN BY LUCK. Nine sites still
assign a fresh dict wholesale to .meta immediately after constructing the
object. All nine are harmless TODAY only because none of them passes a kwarg
that lands in meta, so there is nothing to destroy -- safety by coincidence
of which kwargs those call sites happen to use. Adding one access_mode= to
any of them reinstates the bug with no test failing. Rule 3 flags that
pairing specifically, which converts the coincidence into a guarantee at
zero migration cost.

THREE INSTRUMENT DEFECTS, all found by checking rather than by a failing
test, recorded because each would have produced a confident wrong number:

  * a module-wide name scan flagged an unrelated `for sym in ...` loop in
    go.py, because `sym` was bound to a meta-bearing construction in a
    DIFFERENT function. Rule 3 is now evaluated per scope.
  * `if sym.meta is None: sym.meta = {}` is an INITIALISATION, not a
    replacement. An empty literal destroys nothing.
  * routing a write through the chokepoint made the key VANISH from the
    census (4 -> 1), because only the bypass shape was counted. A fixed key
    could then have been silently down-declared to unaudited. Chokepoint
    calls now count as writers.

Also corrected in the analysis that produced this: a `name=` grep reported
io_boundary and io_primitive as unregistered when the registry spells its
specs POSITIONALLY. Two of the four io keys were already registered; only
io_boundaries and io_mode were not.

MYPY RATCHET: this change breached it by +2 (arg-type 105->106,
attr-defined 3->4), both mine -- an unnarrowed ast.AST and an `Any | None`
into a set[str]. Fixed at source rather than baselined; back to 672, delta 0.

SCOPE STATED RATHER THAN IMPLIED: this lands the mechanism and declares the
five keys there is evidence for. It does NOT audit the other 82, and the
checker prints that number on every clean run so the debt stays visible.

Ref: INV-hazov, INV-virat, INV-zumin, INV-pojib, INV-forim, INV-faput,
WI-vusot, ADR-0024.

